# The Go backend's build artefacts. Kept here rather than in the repository root so the rules
# travel with the module and read against paths that make sense from inside it.

# The compiled server. Rebuilt by scripts/build.sh; nothing outside a release needs it, and it
# is platform-specific, so a committed one would only ever be the wrong architecture.
bin/

# The console, copied in at build time by scripts/build.sh so `go:embed` can bundle it into the
# binary. The source of truth is frontend/, and frontend/dist is itself ignored at the root --
# committing a second copy here would let an image ship a stale bundle.
#
# .gitkeep is the exception and must stay tracked: `go:embed all:dist` refuses a directory that
# does not exist, so without it a fresh clone cannot even compile. scripts/build.sh recreates it
# on every build for the same reason.
internal/web/dist/*
!internal/web/dist/.gitkeep

# Compiled test binaries, from `go test -c`.
*.test

# Profiles and coverage, from `go test -cover` / `-cpuprofile` and friends.
*.out
*.prof
coverage.*

# A local multi-module workspace. It points at whatever directories one developer happens to
# have checked out, so it is never right for anybody else.
go.work
go.work.sum
